Risk tolerance and time horizon.&nbsp;

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:54.660
Here are some common investment options.
One: Stocks.&nbsp;

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:01.260
Investing in stocks involves buying&nbsp;
shares of publicly-traded companies.&nbsp;

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.120
Stocks can provide the potential for&nbsp;
high returns over the long term but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:09.080
they also come with higher&nbsp;
risk than other investments.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:13.440
Two: Bonds.
Investing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.760
bonds involves buying debt securities&nbsp;
issued by governments or corporations.&nbsp;

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:23.640
Bonds provide lower returns than stocks but&nbsp;
they are generally considered less risky.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:27.480
Three: Mutual funds.&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:34.080
A mutual fund is a professionally managed&nbsp;
investment portfolio that pulls money from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:39.780
multiple investors to buy a diversified&nbsp;
mix of stocks, bonds, and other assets.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.660
Four: Exchange traded funds - ETFs.&nbsp;

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:51.900
ETFs are similar to mutual funds but&nbsp;
they trade like stocks on an exchange.&nbsp;

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.180
ETFs provide a convenient way to invest&nbsp;
